				"name": "Soul Ignition",
				"riotSummary": "Locke ignites his soul, gaining Attack Speed and Move Speed, and dealing damage to himself. At the end of the duration, Locke will heal back a portion of the damage he takes during the effect.",
				"riotTooltip": "Locke ignites his own soul, gaining <attackSpeed>{{ attackspeed }} Attack Speed</attackSpeed> and <speed>{{ movespeed }} Move Speed</speed> that decays over {{ decaytimehelper }} seconds.<br /><br />For {{ baseduration }} seconds, he suffers <trueDamage>{{ healthcost*100 }}% current Health true damage</trueDamage> per second but <healing>Heals</healing> back the last <healing>{{ damagerestoreamount }}</healing> damage taken, and an additional <healing>{{ additionalheal }} Health</healing> based on missing Health and time passed, up to a maximum of <healing>{{ maxhealingthreshold }} Health remaining</healing>.<br /><br />Can be <recast>Recast</recast> to end early.{{ spellmodifierdescriptionappend }}",
				"wikiDescription": "Active: Locke ignites his soul for 6 seconds, becoming ghosted and gaining 40% – 70% (based on level) bonus attack speed and 40% (+ 2% per 100 AP) bonus movement speed, with the latter decaying to 20% over 1 second after 1.5 seconds have elapsed.\n\nAdditionally, during the effect he stores an amount of grey health on his health bar equal to 100% of the post-mitigation damage he takes from enemy champions, up to a cap, plus the total amount of health expended from Soul Ignition's health cost. Locke additionally stores up to 40 – 200 (based on level) (+ 20% AP) grey health for himself, based on his missing health and Soul Ignition's elapsed duration. The missing health portion of this additional grey health stored reaches its maximum when his current health is at or below 150 – 450 (based on level) (+ 60% AP).\n\nAfter 0.5 seconds, Soul Ignition can be recast within the duration, and does so automatically afterwards.\n\nRecast: Locke ends Soul Ignition and consumes his grey health to heal for the same amount.",
